                    {
                        "part": "a",
                        "plain_text": {"question": "Complete the Product Rule: d/dx[f(x)g(x)] =", "answer": "f'(x)g(x) + f(x)g'(x)"},
                        "latex": {"question": "Complete the Product Rule: $\\frac{d}{dx}[f(x)g(x)]=$", "answer": "$f'(x)g(x)+f(x)g'(x)$"}
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "name": "Example: Product rule derivative",
                "learning_tag": 2,
                "context_plain": "",
                "context_latex": "",
                "keywords": ["product rule", "derivative", "power rule"],
                "subproblems": [
                    {
                        "part": "a",
                        "plain_text": {
                            "question": "Find d/dx[(1 - cube root of x)(x^2 - 8x)] evaluated at x = 8.",
                            "answer": "d/dx[(1 - cube root of x)(x^2 - 8x)] = -1/3 x^(-2/3)(x^2 - 8x) + (2x - 8)(1 - cube root of x). Plug in x = 8: -1/3 * 8^(-2/3)(8^2 - 8(8)) + (2(8) - 8)(1 - cube root of 8) = -8."
                        },
                        "latex": {
                            "question": "$\\frac{d}{dx}\\left[(1-\\sqrt[3]{x})(x^2-8x)\\right]\\bigg|_{x=8}$",
                            "answer": "$\\frac{d}{dx}\\left[(1-\\sqrt[3]{x})(x^2-8x)\\right]=-\\frac{1}{3}x^{-2/3}(x^2-8x)+(2x-8)(1-\\sqrt[3]{x})$. Plug in $x=8$: $-\\frac{1}{3}8^{-2/3}(8^2-8(8))+(2(8)-8)(1-\\sqrt[3]{8})=-8$."
                        }
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "name": "Exercise: Product rule",
                "learning_tag": 2,
                "context_plain": "Find the following derivatives:",
                "context_latex": "Find the following derivatives:",
                "keywords": ["product rule", "derivative", "evaluating derivatives"],
                "subproblems": [
                    {
                        "part": "a",
                        "plain_text": {"question": "d/dx[(x^2+x+1)(4-2x)]", "answer": "(2x+1)(4-2x) - 2(x^2+x+1)"},
                        "latex": {"question": "$\\frac{d}{dx}[(x^2+x+1)(4-2x)]$", "answer": "$(2x+1)(4-2x)-2(x^2+x+1)$"}
                    },
                    {
                        "part": "b",
                        "plain_text": {
                            "question": "d/dx[(x^3-2x^2)(sqrt(x)+4)] evaluated at x = 1",
                            "answer": "d/dx[(x^3-2x^2)(sqrt(x)+4)] = (3x^2-4x)(sqrt(x)+4) + 1/(2sqrt(x))(x^3-2x^2). Plug in x = 1: (3(1)^2-4(1))(sqrt(1)+4) + 1/(2sqrt(1))((1)^3-2(1)^2) = -11/2."
                        },
                        "latex": {
                            "question": "$\\frac{d}{dx}[(x^3-2x^2)(\\sqrt{x}+4)]\\bigg|_{x=1}$",
                            "answer": "$\\frac{d}{dx}\\left[(x^3-2x^2)(\\sqrt{x}+4)\\right]=(3x^2-4x)(\\sqrt{x}+4)+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}(x^3-2x^2)$. Plug in $x=1$: $(3(1)^2-4(1))(\\sqrt{1}+4)+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}}((1)^3-2(1)^2)=-\\frac{11}{2}$."
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "part": "c",
                        "plain_text": {
                            "question": "d/dt[t * f(t)] evaluated at t = 2, where f(2) = -3 and f'(2) = 7",
                            "answer": "d/dt[t * f(t)] = f(t) + t * f'(t). Plug in t = 2: -3 + 2 * 7 = 11."
                        },
                        "latex": {
                            "question": "$\\frac{d}{dt}\\left[t\\cdot f(t)\\right]\\bigg|_{t=2}$, where $f(2)=-3$ and $f'(2)=7$",
                            "answer": "$\\frac{d}{dt}\\left[t\\cdot f(t)\\right]=f(t)+t\\cdot f'(t)$. Plug in $t=2$: $-3+2\\cdot 7=11$."
                        }
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "name": "Warm-up Exercise 2: Quotient Rule",
                "learning_tag": 2,
